From: Stanislav Malyshev <stas@php.net>
Date: Mon, 27 May 2019 18:04:00 -0700
Subject: Fix bug #77967 - Bypassing open_basedir restrictions via file uris

(cherry picked from commit c34895e837b50213c2bb201c612904342d2bd216)
---
 NEWS                  |   11 +++++++----
 ext/sqlite3/sqlite3.c |    9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/NEWS
+++ b/NEWS
@@ -5,15 +5,18 @@ Backported from 7.1.30
 
 - EXIF:
   . Fixed bug #77988 (heap-buffer-overflow on php_jpg_get16).
-  (CVE-2019-11040) (Stas)
+    (CVE-2019-11040) (Stas)
 
 - GD:
   . Fixed bug #77973 (Uninitialized read in gdImageCreateFromXbm).
-  (CVE-2019-11038) (cmb)
+    (CVE-2019-11038) (cmb)
 
 - Iconv:
   . Fixed bug #78069 (Out-of-bounds read in iconv.c:_php_iconv_mime_decode()
-  due to integer overflow). (CVE-2019-11039). (maris dot adam)
+    due to integer overflow). (CVE-2019-11039). (maris dot adam)
+
+- SQLite:
+  . Fixed bug #77967 (Bypassing open_basedir restrictions via file uris). (Stas)
 
 Backported from 7.1.29
 
@@ -30,7 +33,7 @@ Backported from 7.1.28
   . Fixed bug #77753 (Heap-buffer-overflow in php_ifd_get32s). (CVE-2019-11034)
     (Stas)
   . Fixed bug #77831 (Heap-buffer-overflow in exif_iif_add_value).
-	(CVE-2019-11035) (Stas)
+    (CVE-2019-11035) (Stas)
 
 - SQLite3:
   . Added sqlite3.defensive INI directive. (BohwaZ)
--- a/ext/sqlite3/sqlite3.c
+++ b/ext/sqlite3/sqlite3.c
@@ -2054,6 +2054,15 @@ static int php_sqlite3_authorizer(void *
 				}
 #endif
 
+				if (strncmp(arg3, "file:", 5) == 0) {
+					/* starts with "file:" */
+					if (!arg3[5]) {
+						return SQLITE_DENY;
+					}
+					if (php_check_open_basedir(arg3 + 5)) {
+						return SQLITE_DENY;
+					}
+				}
 				if (php_check_open_basedir(arg3)) {
 					return SQLITE_DENY;
 				}
